<task id="006" project="record-header-and-notepad-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Build LookupField renderer (FR-04)</title>
    <phase>1: Shared Library</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>004</dependencies>
    <blocks>013, 022</blocks>
    <tags>react, typescript, fluent-ui, dataverse</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>New shared component + Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo integration + unit tests</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build LookupField field renderer per FR-04 at src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/fields/LookupField.tsx. Clickable link with entity-icon prefix; on click opens the lookup target via Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo({ pageType: "entityrecord", entityName, entityId }).</prompt>

  <role>Spaarke platform developer. Fluent UI v9 expert; familiar with Xrm.Navigation.</role>

  <goal>LookupField.tsx + tests present; clicking opens Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo with correct entity + record id; zero hex/rgb.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §3.3 — LookupField renders the display name of a lookup value with an entity-icon prefix and makes it clickable. Value shape: { id: string; name: string; entityType: string; } (Xrm.LookupValue-like).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/fields/LookupField.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/fields/index.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/__tests__/fields.test.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens; zero hex/rgb.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">React 16/17 compat.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">FR-04: LookupField clickable, opens target via Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">If Xrm is unavailable (unit-test env), fall back gracefully — do not throw.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/record-header-and-notepad-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-ui-design-system.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/dataverse-queries.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    <existing>None specific to a "clickable lookup with entity-icon prefix" component.</existing>
    <extension>N/A.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without LookupField, every PCF re-implements the icon + link + click-nav pattern. §11 anti-pattern.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Declare ILookupFieldValue { id: string; name: string; entityType: string; iconUrl?: string; } and ILookupFieldProps { label: string; value: ILookupFieldValue | null | undefined; span: 1 | 2 | 3; }.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement LookupField as an FC. Label above; value row = icon (16x16, entity-image from Xrm.Utility.getEntityMetadata or fallback icon) + clickable Link text.</step>
    <step order="3">On Link click: (typeof Xrm !== "undefined" &amp;&amp; Xrm?.Navigation?.navigateTo) — call Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo({ pageType: "entityrecord", entityName: value.entityType, entityId: value.id }). Else, no-op (test env).</step>
    <step order="4">Handle null/undefined value with hyphen "—".</step>
    <step order="5">Export from fields/index.ts.</step>
    <step order="6">Add test cases: renders link with value.name; click invokes mocked Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo; hyphen on null.</step>
    <step order="7">Run tests.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 006 ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/fields/LookupField.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/__tests__/fields.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given value={id, name:"Acme Corp", entityType:"sprk_matter"}, when Link is clicked, then Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo is called with pageType="entityrecord", entityName="sprk_matter", entityId=id.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given value=null, when rendered, then hyphen "—" shown.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given Xrm undefined (test env), when Link is clicked, then no error thrown.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render LookupField in webLightTheme then webDarkTheme</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Icon (currentColor if SVG), link color, and label all adapt via semantic tokens</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>Entity icon resolution: try Xrm.Utility.getEntityMetadata(entityType).then(md =&gt; md.EntityIcon); if unavailable, fallback to a generic Fluent v9 icon (Link24Regular or similar). See spec.md §Assumptions U-02.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files first. Follow task-execute skill.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
